{title: 516 - All the Way}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #516 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 516}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]All the way my savior leads me;
What have [D]I to ask be[G]side?
Can I [C]doubt His tender [D]mercy,
Who thro’ [A]life has been my [D]guide?
Heav’nly [G]peace divinest comfort,
Here by faith in Him to [D]dwell!
For I [G]know whate’er be[C]fall me,
Jesus [G]doeth all [D]things [G]well;
For I know whate’er be[C]fall me,
Jesus [G]doeth all [D]things [G]well;
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]All the way my Savior leads me;
[D]Cheers each winding [G]path I tread;
[C]Gives me grace [D]for every trial,
[A]Feeds me with [D]the living bread;
[G]Though my weary steps may falter,
[D]And my soul athirst may be,
[G]Gushing from the [C]Rock before me,
[G]Lo, a [D]spring of [G]joy I see;
[C]Gushing from the Rock before me,
[G]Lo, a [D]spring of [G]joy I see.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]All the way my Savior leads me;
[D]O the fullness [G]of His love!
[C]Perfect rest to [D]me is promised
[A]In my [D]Father's house above;
[G]When I wake to life immortal,
[D]Wing my flight to realms of day,
[G]This my song [C]through endless ages,
[G]Jesus led [D]me all [G]the way;
[C]This my song through endless ages,
[G]Jesus led [D]me all [G]the way.
{end_of_verse}
